    "id": "ncert.maths.ch01.p006.sqrt2_irrational_proof",
    "text": "Proof that √2 is irrational: Suppose √2 = a/b, where integers a and b are coprime and b is not 0. Squaring gives a^2 = 2b^2, so 2 divides a^2 and hence a. Write a = 2c. Then b^2 = 2c^2, so 2 also divides b. This contradicts a and b being coprime. Therefore √2 is irrational.",
