    "id": "ncert.maths.ch06.p008.basic_proportionality_proof",
    "text": "Basic Proportionality Theorem: In triangle ABC, if D lies on AB, E lies on AC, and DE is parallel to BC, then AD/DB = AE/EC. Proof: using perpendicular heights, area(ADE)/area(BDE) = AD/DB and area(ADE)/area(DEC) = AE/EC. Triangles BDE and DEC share base DE and lie between the same parallels DE and BC, so their areas are equal. Therefore the two side ratios are equal.",
